---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Grand Theft Auto VI — Pre-order & Buying Guide"
  description="Grand Theft Auto VI buying guide: the most-anticipated release, pre-order vs wait, and where to buy the digital version cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Grand Theft Auto VI — Pre-order &amp; Buying Guide</h1>
    <p class="meta">Xbox / PS5 / PC · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong> is the most-anticipated game of the cycle,
      returning to the vice-city-inspired state of Leonida with a new dual-protagonist
      story. Demand will be enormous at launch.
    </p>

    <h2>What we know</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Day-one platforms</strong> — confirmed for current-gen consoles at launch; PC follows later</li>
      <li><strong>Editions</strong> — expect Standard and a premium edition with in-game cash and cosmetic bonuses; no story locks</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-order</strong> — the first reliable way to guarantee a copy at launch</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Pre-order or wait?</h2>
    <p>
      GTA VI will launch at list price with no early discounts — Rockstar games rarely
      drop for years. Pre-order only if you want to play on day one. If you can wait, the
      first real deals follow well after launch. Key stores like Green Man Gaming will
      carry it once available.
    </p>

    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="gmg"
          href="https://www.greenmangaming.com/search/?q=grand+theft+auto+6"
          cta="Check Green Man Gaming"
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Grand+Theft+Auto+VI"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing. Pre-orders
      may not be live yet; check the store for availability.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post { padding: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 720px; }
  .post h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .buy-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
